  "body": {
    "id": "lem:transcript-packing",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(\\mathfrak g_0,\\mathfrak g_1,\\ldots,\\mathfrak g_m\\in\\mathfrak M_{n,K,d,\\tau}\\) have distinct oriented unions, and let \\(\\mathscr D_j=\\{I:|I|\\le s,\\ \\mathcal O_{\\mathfrak g_j}(I)\\ne\\mathcal O_{\\mathfrak g_0}(I)\\}\\). Every exact adaptive recovery tree has depth at least the minimum number of allowed targets whose union hits all \\(\\mathscr D_j\\); in particular, pairwise disjoint nonempty \\(\\mathscr D_j\\) imply depth at least \\(m\\) along the \\(\\mathfrak g_0\\) transcript.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "G-zero",
      "G-alt",
      "model-class",
      "n",
      "K",
      "d",
      "tau",
      "distinguish-family",
      "I",
      "s",
      "O-G",
      "algorithm-A"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:decision-tree",
      "def:distinguishing-families",
      "def:model-class"
    ],
    "justification": "The lemma isolates the exact legality condition missing from informal transfers of single-DAG separating-system lower bounds.",
    "gap": "ShanmugamKocaogluDimakisVishwanath2015SmallInterventions constructs an adaptive total-order transcript for a complete single DAG; it does not ensure simultaneous faithful mixture alternatives.",
    "consumer": "Every lower-bound construction in the frontier can be audited by listing one baseline and its full changed-target families.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix an exact deterministic recovery tree and follow the transcript generated by \\(\\mathfrak g_0\\). Let \\(I_1,\\ldots,I_q\\) be the targets on that root-to-leaf path. If, for some \\(j\\), none of these targets belongs to \\(\\mathscr D_j\\), then\n\\[\n \\mathcal O_{\\mathfrak g_j}(I_h)=\\mathcal O_{\\mathfrak g_0}(I_h),\n \\qquad h=1,\\ldots,q.\n\\]\nInduction on \\(h\\) shows that adaptivity chooses the same next target under \\(\\mathfrak g_j\\) as under \\(\\mathfrak g_0\\), so both models reach the same leaf. That leaf has one output, but \\(\\mathsf T(\\mathfrak g_j)\\ne\\mathsf T(\\mathfrak g_0)\\), contradicting exact recovery. Consequently \\(\\{I_1,\\ldots,I_q\\}\\) intersects every \\(\\mathscr D_j\\), and \\(q\\) is at least the minimum hitting-set cardinality. If the nonempty families \\(\\mathscr D_j\\) are pairwise disjoint, one target can hit at most one of them, so \\(q\\ge m\\).",
